{
  "about": "Phone pairing by number, v1 (POST /api/devices/pair; ~/Khayt-proposals/phone-pairing-code-design.md, C1). The same math as docs/connector-pair.vectors.json with the phone's own prefixes, so neither kind of offer can be replayed as the other. commit = base64 SHA-256('khayt-phone-commit-v1' \\n phonePublic \\n nonce). offerMessage = 'khayt-enrol-phone-v1:' + deviceId + ':' + serverPublic + ':' + commit, signed by the Mac's Ed25519 identity (sig, deterministic). check = first 4 bytes big-endian of SHA-256('khayt-phone-check-v1' \\n deviceId \\n identityPublic \\n serverPublic \\n phonePublic \\n nonce) mod 1000000, zero-padded to 6. pluginPrivateHex / pluginPublic hold the PHONE's X25519 key: the connector file's field names, so one decoder reads both. derivedKey = base64 HKDF-SHA256(X25519 shared secret, salt 'khayt-device-v1', info deviceId, 32), the key both sides sign with once approved. `refuse` lists offers the phone must refuse and reveals the Mac must refuse, each from `first` with one thing wrong. Generated by scripts/write-pair-vectors.js. The nonce is 16 random bytes in real use. Seeds, private keys and nonces here are sample values for tests only.",
